      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Mnemonic function was studied in 105 males with chronic coronary heart disease (CCHD). A reduced volume of memory and intensified inhibition of trace formation was observed in more than 75% of the patients. The degree of memory disorders depended on the form of the CHD course. A combination of drugs dilating the heart vessels with drugs improving metabolism and the brain blood flow resulted in an improvement of mnemonic function."},
